`List Constructor Syntax` is working (2026-10-25)

Parses all 402 graphs at ~/sw/spl/help/SuperCollider/Graph

Parses all 70 graphs at ~/sw/spl/help/SuperCollider/Texture

Parses all 19 programs at ~/sw/spl/help/SuperCollider/Scheduler

```
cd ~/sw/spl/help/SuperCollider/Graph
for i in [A-Z]*.sp ; do echo $i ; stsc3 translate spl st "$i" "/tmp/$i.st" ; done
```

Failures were related to comments.
The lexer was re-written to use the "monad" wrapper.
This changes the way the parser is called, and not all uses have been edited.

Previously failed to parse:

- 1:9 [Allowed]
- p # q [Allowed]
- p.!(q) [Allowed, does renamer run?]
- p.++ [Allowed, does renamer run?]
- 1:k [Rewritten to (1 .. k)]
- (1, 3 .. 33) [Conflict, rewritten to 1:2:33]

The rule for (p, q .. r) introduces a shift-reduce conflict:

    | '(' expression ',' expression '..' expression ')' { splFromThenTo $2 $4 $6 }

The operator methods require a translation function, i.e. ! -> exclamationMark, i.e. sw/spl/ts/operator.ts

Modified to pass:

- Dcv - Time varying feedback delay network.sl
  + s.Neg -> [[]]
  + ctl:: -> ''.kr()
- Jl - Pwm Crossfade.sl
  + let [f1, f2] -> let r
- Jmcc - Bach prelude.sl
  + x[3 4 5] -> x @* [3 4 5]
- Mk - 2206.sl
  + ctl:: -> ''.kr()

p.q in vector_item introduces a shift/reduce conflict
ctl::

* * *

Block comments do not allow either nested comments or the * character.

There could be a distinct comment format that is part of the Ast and may only appear as either:

- class comments (preceding class definition)
- method comments (first element of method body)

"Any kind of sequence can be defined using either left recursion or
right recursion, but you should always use left recursion, because it
can parse a sequence of any number of elements with bounded stack
space."
